# Applies to backend/Dockerfile.ci INSTEAD of the repo-root .dockerignore
# (BuildKit reads <dockerfile-path>.dockerignore when one exists).
#
# The root file excludes backend/tests/, which is right for the production
# image and wrong for this one: with the root rules applied, `uv run pytest`
# collected 0 items and the CI image reported success having run nothing.
# This build needs the repo root as its context to reach surface-manifest.json,
# so it needs its own ignore rules too.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
frontend/
src-tauri/
docs/
# Anchored patterns match the CONTEXT ROOT only, and this context is the repo
# root -- so `.luminary/` alone leaves backend/.luminary/ in the build. That
# directory is a host artefact: 418MB of downloaded model weights, including
# vendored third-party sources that `ruff check .` then lints (8 errors, gate
# red) and a mem_profile the container's DATA_DIR would inherit. A gate whose
# result depends on the developer's working tree is not a gate.
**/.luminary/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.env
**/.env.*
# ...but backend/.env.example is a documentation fixture the suite asserts
# against (test_env_example_documents_the_knobs), so it must survive.
!backend/.env.example
# Same anchoring point, and the same reason: evals/.venv is ~1GB of the
# developer's virtualenv, and the image builds its own with `uv sync`.
**/.venv/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
backend/htmlcov/
backend/.coverage
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
